## External dependencies

OmaIMAPMail itself has no bundled third-party code or libraries. At runtime it
shells out to the following system tools, which are not distributed with this
plugin and are covered by their own respective licenses:

- **python3** (standard library only — `imaplib`, `email`, `ssl`, `json`,
  `threading`, etc. — no pip packages required)
- **secret-tool** (part of `libsecret`) — stores and retrieves IMAP app
  passwords via the system's Secret Service provider (e.g. GNOME Keyring)
- **omarchy-notification-send** — part of Omarchy itself, used to post
  desktop notifications
- **xdg-open** — used to open an account's webmail URL when a message row is
  clicked

All IMAP communication uses Python's standard-library `imaplib`; no
third-party Python packages are required or installed.
